{"name":"Croissant","hex":"#c4ab86","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"croissant","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flaky roll or pastry in a form of a crescent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/croissant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Croissant","blocks":[{"text":"A croissant is a Viennoiserie in a crescent shape made from a laminated yeast dough that sits between a bread and a puff pastry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Croissant-Petr_Kratochvil.jpg/330px-Croissant-Petr_Kratochvil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croissant","wikidata":"Q207832"},{"title":"Croissant (linguistic zone)","blocks":[{"text":"The Croissant is a linguistic transitional zone between the Langue d'oc dialects and the Langue d'oïl dialects, situated in the centre of France where Occitan dialects are spoken that have transitional traits toward French. The name derives from the contours of the zone that resemble a croissant, or crescent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Croissant_%28zone_de_transition_linguistique%29.png/330px-Croissant_%28zone_de_transition_linguistique%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croissant_(linguistic_zone)","wikidata":"Q2426718"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Boulangerie_Viennoise_formerly_Zang%27s_-_1909.jpg/500px-Boulangerie_Viennoise_formerly_Zang%27s_-_1909.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Boulangerie_Viennoise_formerly_Zang%27s_-_1909.jpg/500px-Boulangerie_Viennoise_formerly_Zang%27s_-_1909.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The original Boulangerie Viennoise in 1909 (when it was owned by Phi